      },
      "text": "The nervous system is the most complex structure built by developmental biology. A single neural tube becomes the brain, spinal cord, and peripheral nervous system. Neural development involves the largest number of cell types, the most intricate wiring problem, and the longest developmental timeline (well into adulthood) of any organ system."
    },
    {
